From df1d090f47fdec98ba3c393046d4bd96dfcd5450 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nex <63727521+LuCiLuna@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 23:20:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 061/110] media: i2c: imx789: add the 2176x1224 4x4 binned mode

The stock 240 fps video mode bins 4x4 over the full 8704 pixel width.
Run it at 30 fps by default (longer frame); it needs the stock PLLs, so
link frequency and pixel rate become per mode, and VBLANK is reset to
the mode's default on a mode change. The 4000x3008 crop now records its
352 pixel left offset within the 8704 wide array.

With it libcamera picks a full width sensor mode for 1080p instead of
centre cropping 1920x1080 out of 4000x3008.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
